Pinned but NOT YET BUILT OR LINKED
----------------------------------

Read this heading literally. cmake/PiriCADDependencies.cmake holds an exact
commit SHA for each library below, and nothing include()s that file — not the
root CMakeLists.txt, not a module. No FetchContent runs, no archive is
downloaded, and not one line of any library below is compiled into any PiriCAD
binary today.

This section previously said these were "acquired by CMake FetchContent against
an exact commit SHA", which was false. A NOTICE file is a licence compliance
record, so a claim about what is linked has to be checkable against the build
rather than against the intention. The SHAs are the decision, already reviewed
for licence compatibility; the wiring is the library migration workstream. When
each is genuinely linked it moves to "Currently linked" in the same change.

A moved tag cannot silently change what these resolve to, which is why they are
recorded as SHAs (CLAUDE.md 5.12).

